  "Partitions": {
    "integer_to_list/1": "Require an integer and, for arity2, an integer base2..36; arity1 uses10. Decimal invariant formatting and repeated exact DivRem produce the same sign/uppercase digit sequence, including zero. The list result has fresh cells/immediate characters; binary output is fresh ASCII storage. Invalid types/base raise the original native badarg with complete original arguments/stack.",
    "integer_to_list/2": "Require an integer and, for arity2, an integer base2..36; arity1 uses10. Decimal invariant formatting and repeated exact DivRem produce the same sign/uppercase digit sequence, including zero. The list result has fresh cells/immediate characters; binary output is fresh ASCII storage. Invalid types/base raise the original native badarg with complete original arguments/stack.",
    "integer_to_binary/1": "Require an integer and, for arity2, an integer base2..36; arity1 uses10. Decimal invariant formatting and repeated exact DivRem produce the same sign/uppercase digit sequence, including zero. The list result has fresh cells/immediate characters; binary output is fresh ASCII storage. Invalid types/base raise the original native badarg with complete original arguments/stack.",
    "integer_to_binary/2": "Require an integer and, for arity2, an integer base2..36; arity1 uses10. Decimal invariant formatting and repeated exact DivRem produce the same sign/uppercase digit sequence, including zero. The list result has fresh cells/immediate characters; binary output is fresh ASCII storage. Invalid types/base raise the original native badarg with complete original arguments/stack.",
    "list_to_integer/1": "Validate base2..36 (default10). Preserve the pinned list scanner: exact sign recognition, leading zero skip, low-byte interpretation only for native-small head integers, base-specific short digit threshold, proper-tail requirement. Promote to the strict whole-byte long path exactly after that threshold, resetting to the original list. Parse groups of12 bounded digits with exact balanced BigInteger combination. Fast invalid input uses badarg_with_info; long-path errors use error_with_info. Return the exact signed integer, no input mutation.",
    "binary_to_integer/1": "Validate base and whole-byte bitstring. Match native optional sign/leading-zero scan, immediate all-zero result and remaining-length threshold before digit validation. Strict ASCII digits/signs and exact base arithmetic match the native short/long paths. Fast errors use badarg_with_info; long errors use error_with_info. No whitespace, separators, prefixes or malformed input accepted; no input mutation.",
    "list_to_integer/2": "Validate base2..36 (default10). Preserve the pinned list scanner: exact sign recognition, leading zero skip, low-byte interpretation only for native-small head integers, base-specific short digit threshold, proper-tail requirement. Promote to the strict whole-byte long path exactly after that threshold, resetting to the original list. Parse groups of12 bounded digits with exact balanced BigInteger combination. Fast invalid input uses badarg_with_info; long-path errors use error_with_info. Return the exact signed integer, no input mutation.",
    "binary_to_integer/2": "Validate base and whole-byte bitstring. Match native optional sign/leading-zero scan, immediate all-zero result and remaining-length threshold before digit validation. Strict ASCII digits/signs and exact base arithmetic match the native short/long paths. Fast errors use badarg_with_info; long errors use error_with_info. No whitespace, separators, prefixes or malformed input accepted; no input mutation."
  },
